<title>USA: Italy's 1998 inflation target said credible.</title>
<headline>Italy's 1998 inflation target said credible.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inflation in Italy has reached levels which allow it to see its 1998 target of 1.8 pct as credible, Italy's treasury minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi told reporters on Friday.</p>
<p>He said that inflation would run close to June's 1.5 percent level.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe that 1.5 percent is a historical minimum, and that in the coming months this percentage will be maintained with minimal variations,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Ciampi is here for a summit of the Group of Seven industrialized nations.</p>
</text>
